  -h, --help                   Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell explain
.nf
Explain a stable issue code and how to configure or silence it

Usage: ayame-spell explain [OPTIONS] <CODE>

Arguments:
  <CODE>  Issue code, for example `ja-variant`

Options:
      --lang <LANG>  Explanation language (defaults from LANG) [possible values: en, ja]
  -h, --help         Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell rules
.nf
List every stable issue code

Usage: ayame-spell rules [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --lang <LANG>  Description language (defaults from LANG) [possible values: en, ja]
  -h, --help         Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell completions
.nf
Generate a shell completion script on standard output

Usage: ayame-spell completions <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>  [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell lsp
.nf
Run the LSP server (used by editor integrations)

Usage: ayame-spell lsp [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --stdio  Use standard input/output transport. Accepted for client compatibility; stdio is
               always the transport
  -h, --help   Print help
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ayame-spell.toml
Project configuration.
.TP
.I ayame-words.txt
Project word list used by the default configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means no findings, 1 means findings were reported, and 2 means an error occurred.
